A Problem abstract class to extract the questions from some external api

It should take input as the number of questions to fetch and the difficulty level

The number of questions can be between 1 to 50

There will be 4 difficulty levels: easy, medium, hard, and custom

If custom is chosen then the questions get harder based on the users performance.

(We can set some performance criteria here, initially we can do like 50% easy, 30% medium and 20% hard)

The type of questions can be multiple choice or true/false or a mix of both (this can be another input parameter)

Also we can have different categories like General Knowledge, Science, History, etc. (this can be another input parameter)

Also fill in the blanks and numerical can be added

The problem source currently to be used is Open Trivia DB (https://opentdb.com/api_config.php)


First we will develop whether this works for one user using Tkinter

And then we will try the player vs player mode

We should use " OOP principles—encapsulation, inheritance, polymorphism,
and abstraction—through a layered application architecture " and also provide a UML diagram for the same.

And also we should have separate modules for abstract

ALso we should write unit tests for the same.